  "description": "The \u0027dss_meanings_cached\u0027 dataset is designed to provide a structured way to categorize and detect patterns or values in various data elements, such as incidents or devices. Each entry in the dataset is uniquely identified by an \u0027id\u0027, which helps in distinguishing between different elements like incident IDs or device IDs. The \u0027label\u0027 column categorizes these elements, often prefixing them with \u0027OUTAGE\u0027 to indicate their relevance to outage-related data. The \u0027detectable\u0027 column is a boolean indicator that specifies whether a particular pattern or value can be detected, which is crucial for data analysis and pattern recognition tasks. The \u0027type\u0027 column differentiates between data that is a pattern or a list of values, providing clarity on the nature of the data. The \u0027normalizationMode\u0027 column describes the method used for normalizing the data, ensuring consistency across the dataset. Lastly, the \u0027description\u0027 column offers additional context or details about each entry, enhancing the understanding of the data. This dataset is particularly useful for data scientists and engineers working on data normalization, pattern detection, and categorization tasks in fields like network management and incident response.",
